---
/**
 * THE HANDOFF — sport ends, achievements continue elsewhere.
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS. Audit §4 asks for achievements "showcased separately", so the
 * record moved off this page to /beyond-academics/achievements/. A reader who
 * has just read about facilities, games, participation, houses and coaching is
 * exactly the reader who now wants the medals — and without this band the page
 * would simply stop, with the thing they were building towards nowhere in sight
 * and no link to it.
 *
 * IT NAMES THE THREE MAJORS RATHER THAN SAYING "see our achievements". A link
 * that states what is behind it is worth following; a link that does not, is
 * not. Every one of the three is published — see data/achievements.ts.
 */
---

<section class="sxa" aria-labelledby="sxa-title">
  <div class="u-container">
    <a class="sxa__card" href="/beyond-academics/achievements/">
      <div class="sxa__body">
        {/* Visitor-facing copy, not project language. This read "Shown
            separately, as the audit asks" — accurate about WHY the section
            moved, and meaningless to a parent, who has never seen the audit. */}
        <p class="sxa__eyebrow t-label">Beyond the field</p>
        <h2 class="sxa__h" id="sxa-title">And then the results</h2>
        <p class="sxa__b">
          An international robotics placing in Kuala Lumpur, second in Uttar Pradesh at the
          National School Innovation Awards, and CBSE Cluster V Kho-Kho gold — with the full
          sporting and academic record behind them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <span class="sxa__go">
        Achievements
        <svg width="15" height="10" viewBox="0 0 14 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 1l4 4-4 4M13 5H0" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" />
        </svg>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sxa {
    padding-block: var(--sb-section-y);
    background: var(--sb-paper);
  }

  /* THE WHOLE BAND IS THE LINK, not a paragraph with a link at the end of it —
     a 900px target rather than a 90px one, which matters most on a phone. */
  .sxa__card {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 64px);
    padding: clamp(28px, 3vw, 52px);
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-3);
    background: var(--sb-violet-ink);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    transition: transform var(--sb-dur-link) var(--sb-ease), box-shadow var(--sb-dur-link) ease;
  }

  .sxa__card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: 0 28px 56px -26px rgba(28, 14, 8, 0.5);
  }

  .sxa__card:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--sb-lime); outline-offset: 4px; }

  .sxa__eyebrow { color: var(--sb-lime); }

  .sxa__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-4);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.032em;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .sxa__b {
    margin-top: var(--sb-4);
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: var(--sb-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  }

  .sxa__go {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--sb-4);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 14px 24px;
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-full);
    background: var(--sb-violet);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: var(--sb-body-sm);
    transition: background var(--sb-dur-btn) ease, gap var(--sb-dur-btn) var(--sb-ease);
  }

  .sxa__card:hover .sxa__go { background: var(--sb-violet-dark); gap: var(--sb-6); }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .sxa__card { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>
